      "message": "Hello,\n\nI was helping Pieter[0] to investigate the root-cause for their crashes. The first crash was triggered by mid-convergence issue in their setup - there was a route over a BVI that forwarded traffic to a vxlan tunnel and the vtep dst was looped again to the BVI and therefore the tunnel again and so on. So, the first packet triggered the infinite encapsulation issue (vxlan4-encap -\u003e ip4-rewrite -\u003e ... l2-input .. l2-output -\u003e vxlan4-encap and so on). While this is an obviously wrong configuration - vpp shouldn\u0027t crash.\n\nthis patch adds check for available headroom in vxlan plugin.\n\n[0] - https://lists.fd.io/g/vpp-dev/topic/26_06_worker_crashes_with/121592811",
